  "<section class=\"course-page\" id=\"lesson-08\" data-chapter11-complete=\"pns\" hidden=\"\">\n<div class=\"p2-topic\">\n<header class=\"page-header\">\n<p class=\"eyebrow\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-589\">Learn \u00b7 Chapter 11</p>\n<h1 data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-590\">Peripheral control</h1>\n<p class=\"lesson-question\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-591\">How are voluntary and involuntary activities controlled?</p>\n<div class=\"goal-strip\"><div><p class=\"section-label\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l08-setup-01\">Learning goal</p><p data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l08-setup-02\">I can compare somatic and autonomic control and describe fight-or-flight and rest-and-digest responses.</p></div>\n<div><p class=\"section-label\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l08-setup-03\">Before you begin</p><p data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l08-setup-04\">Review the CNS, PNS and the receptor-to-effector pathway.</p></div></div>\n<details class=\"page-guide\">\n<summary data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l08-guide-summary\"><strong>How to complete this lesson</strong> \u2014 Learn \u2192 practise \u2192 required check \u2192 finish</summary>\n<div>\n<ol>\n<li data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l08-guide-01\"><strong>Start with the lesson.</strong> Read the learning goal and \u201cBefore you begin,\u201d then work through the explanation, diagrams and examples below. The embedded textbook is optional support: open it when you want another explanation or a closer look at a figure.</li>\n<li data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l08-guide-02\"><strong>Use the learning goal and starting reminder.</strong> The learning goal above tells you what you must be able to explain. Read \u201cBefore you begin\u201d next to connect this lesson to what you already know.</li>\n<li data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l08-guide-03\"><strong>Work through the online lesson in order.</strong> Read each teaching section and study its diagrams, examples and comparisons. Select an underlined biology term when you need its meaning. Use the video or Vocabulary help when an idea is still unclear.</li>\n<li data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l08-guide-04\"><strong>Complete the required chapter check.</strong> Open the check near the bottom and select Start. For multiple choice, select Check answer; a correct answer unlocks the related writing. Answer in your own words and select Save written response for every response box.</li>\n<li data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l08-guide-05\"><strong>Submit only when the required work is complete.</strong> Check that every required item has been attempted and every written response is saved. Then select Submit and finish. This stops the timer, records the completed run in All My Work and updates chapter progress.</li>\n<li data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l08-guide-06\"><strong>Use optional practice only when it helps.</strong> Optional source practice and Practice &amp; Review activities can help you study, but they do not count toward the 12 required chapter checks.</li>\n</ol>\n<p data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l08-guide-07\"><strong>Expected work:</strong> complete the lesson and submit the required chapter check. Use optional reading, videos and practice when they help. Drafts save automatically as you work in this browser.</p>\n</div>\n</details>\n<div class=\"textbook-band\"><div><p class=\"section-label\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l08-setup-05\">Optional embedded reading</p><p data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l08-setup-06\"><strong>Chapter 11 \u00b7 pp. 396\u2013399</strong></p></div><a class=\"text-link\" href=\"#textbook-library\" data-book-page=\"37\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l08-setup-07\">Open at p. 396</a></div>\n<p class=\"lesson-term-strip\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l08-teacher-voice-terms\"><strong>Key terms:</strong> somatic \u00b7 autonomic \u00b7 sympathetic \u00b7 parasympathetic</p>\n<details class=\"lesson-vocabulary-help\">\n<summary data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l08-teacher-voice-vocab-summary\">Vocabulary help</summary>\n<section class=\"lesson-words\" aria-labelledby=\"lesson-08-anchor-words\"><p class=\"section-label\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l08-setup-08\">Key terms</p><h2 id=\"lesson-08-anchor-words\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l08-setup-09\">Words for this lesson</h2><p data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l08-setup-10\">Use these definitions when you need help with a term.</p><dl>\n<div><dt><button type=\"button\" class=\"bio-term\" data-bio-term=\"pns\" data-bio-term-route=\"lesson-08\" aria-haspopup=\"dialog\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l08-setup-11\">PNS</button></dt><dd data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l08-setup-12\">nerves connecting the CNS with the rest of the body</dd></div>\n<div><dt><button type=\"button\" class=\"bio-term\" data-bio-term=\"somatic nervous system\" data-bio-term-route=\"lesson-08\" aria-haspopup=\"dialog\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l08-setup-13\">somatic nervous system</button></dt><dd data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l08-setup-14\">the system that carries somatic sensory information and controls skeletal muscles</dd></div>\n<div><dt><button type=\"button\" class=\"bio-term\" data-bio-term=\"autonomic nervous system\" data-bio-term-route=\"lesson-08\" aria-haspopup=\"dialog\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l08-setup-15\">autonomic nervous system</button></dt><dd data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l08-setup-16\">the system that controls involuntary activity in organs and glands</dd></div>\n<div><dt><button type=\"button\" class=\"bio-term\" data-bio-term=\"sympathetic division\" data-bio-term-route=\"lesson-08\" aria-haspopup=\"dialog\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l08-setup-17\">sympathetic division</button></dt><dd data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l08-setup-18\">the autonomic division involved in fight-or-flight</dd></div>\n</dl></section>\n<details class=\"lesson-term-inventory\"><summary data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l08-setup-19\">More vocabulary for this lesson</summary><div><section aria-labelledby=\"lesson-08-all-terms\"><h3 id=\"lesson-08-all-terms\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l08-setup-20\">Lesson vocabulary</h3><dl><div class=\"lesson-term-row\"><dt data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l08-setup-21\">PNS \u00b7 CNS \u00b7 somatic nervous system \u00b7 autonomic nervous system \u00b7 voluntary control \u00b7 sympathetic division \u00b7 parasympathetic division \u00b7 autonomic balance \u00b7 opposing effects \u00b7 effector \u00b7 response \u00b7 homeostasis \u00b7 acetylcholine \u00b7 norepinephrine \u00b7 epinephrine \u00b7 hormone \u00b7 evidence</dt><dd data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l08-setup-22\">Select an underlined term for its definition. Your vocabulary writing is saved in Process Collection.</dd></div></dl></section></div></details>\n</details>\n</header>\n",
